 {:db/id "q-49468/ma-source-field/7a3edbd5e0663fb8769d1f548cc9b354b411dc737c6534ac672c089a0588a301" :answer-field/id #uuid "69629315-77cc-510c-b6be-75d926e5d966" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-49468/ma-source-field/7a3edbd5e0663fb8769d1f548cc9b354b411dc737c6534ac672c089a0588a301/7a5f3ce7b330c10d2531acacab99f1128dd2a7f3e27823a835266036416059c0" "q-49468/ma-source-field/7a3edbd5e0663fb8769d1f548cc9b354b411dc737c6534ac672c089a0588a301/1713b69c60f2939a9b17aad2130db2fc7631f64062cf3744498de211a148b0fb" "q-49468/ma-source-field/7a3edbd5e0663fb8769d1f548cc9b354b411dc737c6534ac672c089a0588a301/ae0b08f9eadea9dc733167885b6ab02db28a1c5037f474d3b2ef0fd6cdf8b81c" "q-49468/ma-source-field/7a3edbd5e0663fb8769d1f548cc9b354b411dc737c6534ac672c089a0588a301/d3553828190ba618bd96e797e7e0114fa8895d7e7dc1e44c21ce6a856e4e531d" "q-49468/ma-source-field/7a3edbd5e0663fb8769d1f548cc9b354b411dc737c6534ac672c089a0588a301/a20ddc92c278bfee059db77148671abcf7188a9a7082d11524c223e760613926"] :answer-field/correct "q-49468/ma-source-field/7a3edbd5e0663fb8769d1f548cc9b354b411dc737c6534ac672c089a0588a301/d3553828190ba618bd96e797e7e0114fa8895d7e7dc1e44c21ce6a856e4e531d" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-49468" :question/id #uuid "2058ea27-d95b-5f37-8b22-5c724bfe6f2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-49468" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt[5]{{(s+1)}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}s=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int {(s+1)}^{-3/5}\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nNow, we let  $u=s+1.$ Then differentiating with respect to $s$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}s}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}s=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $u$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {(s+1)}^{-3/5}\\,\\text{d}s & =\\int {u}^{-3/5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2/5}{u}^{2/5}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{u}^{2/5}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{(s+1)}^{2/5}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\sqrt[5]{{(s+1)}^{2}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}[\\frac{5}{2}\\sqrt[5]{{(s+1)}^{2}}+C] & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}[\\sqrt[5]{{(s+1)}^{2}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}[{(s+1)}^{2/5}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}{(s+1)}^{-3/5}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(s+1)+0 \\\\  & ={(s+1)}^{-3/5}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[5]{{(s+1)}^{3}}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-49468/ma-source-field/7a3edbd5e0663fb8769d1f548cc9b354b411dc737c6534ac672c089a0588a301"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
