 {:db/id "q-70703" :question/id #uuid "10f06241-6aca-53ce-a0c6-b82287839cf2" :question/math-academy-id "q-70703" :question/problem "What are the dimensions of $ML$, if $M$ is a $4\\times 3$ matrix and $L$ is a $3\\times 6$ matrix?" :question/worked-solution "There are $3$ columns in $M$ and $3$ rows in $L.$ Since the number of columns in $M$ equals the number of rows in $L,$ the matrices $M$ and $L$ are conformable for multiplication, and $ML$ is a $4\\times 6$ matrix:\n\n$$\n{M}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{L}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 6}={ML}_{4\\times 6}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-70703/ma-source-field/b6bc4ba00e03d9ab3f08d6b4d62d17bce476dd265aabd38afdb5f4b5a7323588"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
