 {:db/id "q-72424/ma-source-field/a545d198b9ccb422d599aaf8831a744e861bc745094d56d80b18241ee26e0f4a" :answer-field/id #uuid "6ee57767-a470-5ed2-888e-e7479cb9accb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-72424/ma-source-field/a545d198b9ccb422d599aaf8831a744e861bc745094d56d80b18241ee26e0f4a/7529b7133782017e05b48223dfcc8144183a9209d0523b2879f2e66d86c3a9f9" "q-72424/ma-source-field/a545d198b9ccb422d599aaf8831a744e861bc745094d56d80b18241ee26e0f4a/1ff9a5e93a9ba9ced3e62c1051de16084073dc64c3f9eceb5b64571c2b31b0ab" "q-72424/ma-source-field/a545d198b9ccb422d599aaf8831a744e861bc745094d56d80b18241ee26e0f4a/249ea44cb4cacbb3b17fab795934c30f760ba3239a91f6479b8a6943eba80464" "q-72424/ma-source-field/a545d198b9ccb422d599aaf8831a744e861bc745094d56d80b18241ee26e0f4a/ebde65345d79b2dfdff9a01b83d42555a1df95902af4433ec5edb5a8c4fab2d5" "q-72424/ma-source-field/a545d198b9ccb422d599aaf8831a744e861bc745094d56d80b18241ee26e0f4a/de9f392d1940f7db3083b0fe123bd5dc60da2632316f2d04d563ccd6728ff4ca"] :answer-field/correct "q-72424/ma-source-field/a545d198b9ccb422d599aaf8831a744e861bc745094d56d80b18241ee26e0f4a/1ff9a5e93a9ba9ced3e62c1051de16084073dc64c3f9eceb5b64571c2b31b0ab" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-72424" :question/id #uuid "8c75bb9c-44e2-5f73-9a68-3c296ae237a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-72424" :question/problem "$\\int 16(7-2x)^{7}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=7-2x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 16(7-2x)^{7}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 16{u}^{7}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =16\\int {u}^{7}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =16\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})\\int {u}^{7}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-8\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{8}}{8}+C \\\\  & =-{u}^{8}+C \\\\  & =-(7-2x)^{8}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-(7-2x)^{8}+C] & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(7-2x)^{8}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-8(7-2x)^{7}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7-2x)+0 \\\\  & =-8(7-2x)^{7}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =16(7-2x)^{7}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-72424/ma-source-field/a545d198b9ccb422d599aaf8831a744e861bc745094d56d80b18241ee26e0f4a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
