 {:db/id "q-74650/ma-source-field/3786831e217eb031f10c3c1dff87ed301bb2000b1e5298c99515304f8f641b57" :answer-field/id #uuid "ce520123-e722-5fc8-b4b5-0ce963a1fe4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-74650/ma-source-field/3786831e217eb031f10c3c1dff87ed301bb2000b1e5298c99515304f8f641b57/40a1a273986776af283f3fe5271d8cce9b3f9fa9c2c7fc5bf8516dd5a30de4b0" "q-74650/ma-source-field/3786831e217eb031f10c3c1dff87ed301bb2000b1e5298c99515304f8f641b57/fec406b037c336df04ddc47abb8cf02e3ae194404415f3659041d4a99c636727" "q-74650/ma-source-field/3786831e217eb031f10c3c1dff87ed301bb2000b1e5298c99515304f8f641b57/248b51d8dbaf80f78dea125bdb05eb0e56e973e920360179ea3a5b84faaf510d" "q-74650/ma-source-field/3786831e217eb031f10c3c1dff87ed301bb2000b1e5298c99515304f8f641b57/a9d809426690fc6065e8673c85a555723d4ab72d745ec39834681473e579f93a" "q-74650/ma-source-field/3786831e217eb031f10c3c1dff87ed301bb2000b1e5298c99515304f8f641b57/137501af3ee859ebc04c1ab0d44d1b8c87d2d9c5abf6c7a5030f36ed2b1cd52b"] :answer-field/correct "q-74650/ma-source-field/3786831e217eb031f10c3c1dff87ed301bb2000b1e5298c99515304f8f641b57/a9d809426690fc6065e8673c85a555723d4ab72d745ec39834681473e579f93a" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-74650" :question/id #uuid "2b1df7fe-03a7-50e4-93e7-ab9ba910308e" :question/math-academy-id "q-74650" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is consistent dependent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x+6y=4 \\\\  & x+(k+1)y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & 4 \\\\ 1 & k+1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & 4 \\\\ 1 & k+1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & 4 \\\\ 0 & k-2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x+6y=4 \\\\  & (k-2)y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is consistent dependent if it has infinitely many solutions. For the system to have infinitely many solutions, it must have at least one free variable.\n\nIf $k=2,$ then the second equation is $0=0,$ which is true for any value of $y.$ So, we can remove this equation from the system. As a result, the system will contain only one equation, $2x+6y=4.$  \n\nThen, the basic variable will be $x,$ and we will have a free variable $y.$ That means the system will have infinitely many solutions.\n\nTherefore, our system is consistent dependent when $k=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-74650/ma-source-field/3786831e217eb031f10c3c1dff87ed301bb2000b1e5298c99515304f8f641b57"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
