 {:db/id "q-75024" :question/id #uuid "3d8eef93-735e-5ee8-8363-b800d4ca0ad1" :question/math-academy-id "q-75024" :question/problem "Given the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 8 & -4\\end{aligned}]$, find a basis of $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reduce the matrix $A$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 8 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=0$ is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{3}+2{x}_{4}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe general solution is ${x}_{1}=4{x}_{3}-2{x}_{4},$ where ${x}_{2},$ ${x}_{3},$ and ${x}_{4}$ are free variables. Therefore, if $x\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{3}-2{x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{4} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{4}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis implies that \n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nis a basis of $\\text{Null}(A)$ since it is a linearly independent set and its vectors generate $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-75024/ma-source-field/357d1e60ce5d27c246fb7dee7683b69b06e22289bdaea89949531d3f21eea3e5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
