 {:db/id "q-75025/ma-source-field/1166a66061b1a7d0ccb764d2ad99de3d761c0baaa0ded4458bdb6abaef988238" :answer-field/id #uuid "733527a3-aaaa-58a9-a078-bc2475c131cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-75025/ma-source-field/1166a66061b1a7d0ccb764d2ad99de3d761c0baaa0ded4458bdb6abaef988238/6b7e07594c8480d7ff7c3b053b30beff09b309eb8e24fcdd35f2f542c523b790" "q-75025/ma-source-field/1166a66061b1a7d0ccb764d2ad99de3d761c0baaa0ded4458bdb6abaef988238/dfc9de37f8d4b24e7fa4cf8ab473312db52fba663b2a4e0577ccf1a5366c1d0d" "q-75025/ma-source-field/1166a66061b1a7d0ccb764d2ad99de3d761c0baaa0ded4458bdb6abaef988238/4f27f86fcf27784a36381433a8306a8c4a67474f9f477ec5d5a785c4bd381085" "q-75025/ma-source-field/1166a66061b1a7d0ccb764d2ad99de3d761c0baaa0ded4458bdb6abaef988238/d1cedaaa9334d1906d21b055461bce9449b8a35cd9611a41f944986623d577ae" "q-75025/ma-source-field/1166a66061b1a7d0ccb764d2ad99de3d761c0baaa0ded4458bdb6abaef988238/47ca9b38dee9e032667a6d1f10eb87228e6fa93da8cb157c8506929d2e22ee67"] :answer-field/correct "q-75025/ma-source-field/1166a66061b1a7d0ccb764d2ad99de3d761c0baaa0ded4458bdb6abaef988238/6b7e07594c8480d7ff7c3b053b30beff09b309eb8e24fcdd35f2f542c523b790" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-75025" :question/id #uuid "505e94a9-1916-5eb5-8401-0ae000faefd5" :question/math-academy-id "q-75025" :question/problem "Given the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$, find a basis of $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reduce the matrix $A$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=0$ is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{3}-7{x}_{4}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}-3{x}_{4}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe general solution is ${x}_{1}=-4{x}_{3}+7{x}_{4}$ and ${x}_{2}=-{x}_{3}+3{x}_{4},$ where ${x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{4}$ are free variables. Therefore, if $x\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4{x}_{3}+7{x}_{4} \\\\ -{x}_{3}+3{x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}7{x}_{4} \\\\ 3{x}_{4} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{4}[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3},{x}_{4}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis implies that \n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nis a basis of $\\text{Null}(A)$ since it is a linearly independent set and its vectors generate $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-75025/ma-source-field/1166a66061b1a7d0ccb764d2ad99de3d761c0baaa0ded4458bdb6abaef988238"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
