 {:db/id "q-80810" :question/id #uuid "fb01c25e-4ce1-591f-b1b8-8c295e973407" :question/math-academy-id "q-80810" :question/problem "Which statement is **not** true?" :question/worked-solution "If $A⊆B,$ then $A$ is a subset of $B,$ meaning that every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nAmong the given choices, only $Z⊆N$ is not true. This statement is not true because not every integer is a natural number.  For example, we have $-1\\in Z$ but $-1\\notin N.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80810/ma-source-field/75632f6a3a952c667732f1e5141a52b1ee09576edfa7e1f75aac5f2e6cb8dc01"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
