 {:db/id "q-80917/ma-source-field/8229ea581279db4b55bb24c0e8bf1faeaae4dda96f8a7f01ff1ebeb68828a563" :answer-field/id #uuid "d2967834-56c7-54af-a045-1eb688f37565" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-80917/ma-source-field/8229ea581279db4b55bb24c0e8bf1faeaae4dda96f8a7f01ff1ebeb68828a563/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-80917/ma-source-field/8229ea581279db4b55bb24c0e8bf1faeaae4dda96f8a7f01ff1ebeb68828a563/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f" "q-80917/ma-source-field/8229ea581279db4b55bb24c0e8bf1faeaae4dda96f8a7f01ff1ebeb68828a563/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-80917/ma-source-field/8229ea581279db4b55bb24c0e8bf1faeaae4dda96f8a7f01ff1ebeb68828a563/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-80917/ma-source-field/8229ea581279db4b55bb24c0e8bf1faeaae4dda96f8a7f01ff1ebeb68828a563/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :answer-field/correct "q-80917/ma-source-field/8229ea581279db4b55bb24c0e8bf1faeaae4dda96f8a7f01ff1ebeb68828a563/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-80917" :question/id #uuid "8179a1bc-9dd2-5c9c-a7dd-3de3a7cd250c" :question/math-academy-id "q-80917" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear differential equations given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]x(t).\n$$\n\nGiven that the solution to the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ a\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}+{c}_{2}([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ a\\end{aligned}]t{e}^{5t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}),\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R,\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince $A$ is upper-triangular, the repeated eigenvalue is $\\lambda =5$ (of multiplicity two).\nFor this eigenvalue, we get \n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n$v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince we have a repeated eigenvalue $\\lambda $ and only one linearly independent eigenvector $v$, the solution of the system of differential equations is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}v{e}^{\\lambda t}+{c}_{2}(vt{e}^{\\lambda t}+w{e}^{\\lambda t}\\,),\n$$\n\nwhere $w$ is a solution to the equation $(A-\\lambda I)w=v.$\n\nTo find $w,$ we solve the equation $(A-\\lambda I)w=v$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A-\\lambda I)w & =v \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}5-5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5-5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1} \\\\ {w}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1} \\\\ {w}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last equality allows us to form the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0{w}_{1}+2{w}_{2}=1 \\\\ 0{w}_{1}+0{w}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n{w}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nThe variable ${w}_{1}$ is a free variable. Setting ${w}_{1}=0,$ we get \n\n$$\nw=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}+{c}_{2}([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]t{e}^{5t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}),\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nFinally, we see that $a=0,b=\\frac{1}{2},$ and $a+b=\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80917/ma-source-field/8229ea581279db4b55bb24c0e8bf1faeaae4dda96f8a7f01ff1ebeb68828a563"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
